# Markdown is deliberately out of scope for now. Prettier rewraps prose, which
# is where it is most opinionated and least useful, and it would bury the real
# diff. Remove this line when you want docs formatted too.
*.md

# Generated by Next on every build, and it says so in its own header: "This
# file should not be edited". Prettier wants single quotes where Next writes
# double, so formatting it starts a fight that is lost again on the next
# build — which is exactly what happened: `format` rewrote it, `next build`
# regenerated it, and CI failed on the version that got committed.
# eslint.config.mjs already ignores it for the same reason.
next-env.d.ts

# Scratch written by browser-driving agents (Playwright MCP snapshots and
# screenshots). Git-ignored on this machine only, so prettier — which walks the
# tree itself — is what turns a browser pass into a red `verify`.
.playwright-mcp
